  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Western Area (Rural &amp; Urban) Floods Response</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">In response to ongoing flooding in Freetown and Western Area (Rural and Urban) districts, CAFOD and Caritas Freetown (CF) will address immediate needs of the affected population, in close collaboration with other humanitarian partners. CF undertook a joint needs assessment with National Disaster Management Agency and conducted go-and-see visits to understand the needs of flood-affected communities which revealed critical humanitarian needs (shelter, water scarcity, food shortages, non-food items).  Community leaders and volunteers underscored the need for essential resources: clean water and multi-purpose cash transfers to access basic essential needs e.g. food and NFIs. In coordination with WASH actors in the same target communities. CAFOD and CF will focus on Multiple Purpose Cash Assistance (MPCA) interventions based on the needs assessment (Caritas Freetown has an ongoing MoU with MPCA service provider). The WASH actors will build on the experience and approaches developed during COVID-19 pandemic to provide hygiene and sanitation messages in affected communities to mitigate the risk of water borne diseases</narrative>
  </description>
